{#-
  sitemap.xml (P1.10). PLAN §3:
    - every <loc> is an indexable page — membership is decided by the ONE
      shared macro (PLAN §2.3), never re-implemented here;
    - lastmod is emitted ONLY when it is meaningful (see below);
    - no <changefreq> / <priority> (Google ignores them);
    - the sitemap never lists itself.

  LASTMOD IS OPTIONAL AND MUST NOT LIE
  sitemaps.org: <lastmod> is optional, W3C Datetime, "if desired" without
  the time portion (https://www.sitemaps.org/protocol.html). Google uses the
  value only "if it's consistently and verifiably" accurate, and it "should
  reflect the date and time of the last significant update to the page"
  (https://developers.google.com/search/docs/crawling-indexing/sitemaps/build-sitemap).

  So lastmod = the page's own revision signal, in this order:
    1. front-matter `updated` (real editorial revision) — string or Date;
    2. front-matter `date` ONLY for a POST (its publication date is a
       genuine, meaningful signal);
    3. otherwise the element is OMITTED.

  Pages without a real date — most importantly / (src/pages/index.njk has
  no front-matter `date`, so Eleventy falls back to the FILE MTIME) — must
  not get one. This shipped once as a BLOCKER-adjacent defect: every rebuild
  rewrote the home page's <lastmod> with a new mtime, i.e. the sitemap told
  crawlers the home page had changed on every single build. A lastmod that
  changes without a content change trains crawlers to ignore lastmod
  everywhere in the file.

  The home page is a rolling archive: it genuinely changes whenever a post
  ships, so it is the one non-post page that gets a real lastmod — the
  newest publishable post's date (collections.newestPost, PLAN §2.2). That
  is stable across rebuilds and true.
-#}
{% import "partials/indexing.njk" as indexing %}
{%- set siteLastmod = collections.newestPost[0].date.toISOString() if collections.newestPost | length > 0 else undefined -%}
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">
{%- for item in collections.pagesAll -%}
{%- set indexable = indexing.is_indexable(item, collections, item.data.robots) -%}
{#- Post shape: /posts/<slug>/ — parts ["", "posts", "<slug>", ""]. The bare
      /posts/ index has parts[2] == "" and /posts/page/N/ has parts[3] ==
      "page", so both fall through to the no-lastmod branch. -#}
{%- set parts = item.url.split("/") -%}
{%- set isPostItem = parts[1] == "posts" and parts[2] and parts[2] != "page" and parts[3] == "" -%}
{%- if indexable == "true" and not item.data.draft -%}
{#- `updated` may be a string (PLAN §4) or a Date (YAML auto-parse). -#}
{%- set lastmod = undefined -%}
{%- if item.data.updated -%}
{%- if item.data.updated is string -%}
{%- set lastmod = item.data.updated -%}
{%- else -%}
{%- set lastmod = item.data.updated.toISOString() -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- elif item.url == "/" and siteLastmod -%}
{#- Home is a rolling archive: lastmod = newest publishable post. -#}
{%- set lastmod = siteLastmod -%}
{%- elif isPostItem and item.date -%}
{%- set lastmod = item.date.toISOString() -%}
{%- endif -%}
  <url>
    <loc>{{ site.url }}{{ item.url }}</loc>
{%- if lastmod %}
    <lastmod>{{ lastmod }}</lastmod>
{%- endif %}
  </url>
{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
</urlset>
